Package: eruditto
Version: 0.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libx11-6, libgl1, libxcb1, libxau6, libxdmcp6, libbsd0, xclip, xdotool, xdg-utils, desktop-file-utils, libnotify-bin
Maintainer: Darwin Ovalle <dovallep@unal.edu.co>
Description: Ditto-inspired clipboard manager for Linux
 Eruditto monitors your clipboard history and lets you recall,
 search, and paste previous clips — including images — via a
 lightweight popup triggered by a global hotkey (default
 Ctrl+Shift+Z).
 .
 Features:
  - Text and image clipboard history
  - Full-text search (FTS5) with slash-mode filtering
  - Pin important clips so they survive history trimming
  - Auto-paste into the previously focused app
  - Configurable global hotkey
  - System tray with quick actions
  - Start-on-boot (XDG autostart)
  - Dark and light theme support
Homepage: https://github.com/darwinovalle/eruditto
License: MIT
